<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Graph import on Apache HugeGraph</title><link>https://hugegraph-oink.staged.apache.org/docs/quickstart/toolchain/import/</link><description>Recent content in Graph import on Apache HugeGraph</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 02:36:05 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://hugegraph-oink.staged.apache.org/docs/quickstart/toolchain/import/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Import Graph Data with SeaTunnel Sink</title><link>https://hugegraph-oink.staged.apache.org/docs/quickstart/toolchain/import/hugegraph-seatunnel-connector/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://hugegraph-oink.staged.apache.org/docs/quickstart/toolchain/import/hugegraph-seatunnel-connector/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;SeaTunnel connects data sources such as databases and Kafka to HugeGraph. The connector has two parts: &lt;strong&gt;Source reads data and Sink writes data&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;sup&gt;[1][2]&lt;/sup&gt;, with SeaTunnel transform components available between them. To export or migrate data from HugeGraph, see the &lt;a href="https://hugegraph-oink.staged.apache.org/docs/quickstart/toolchain/export-migration/hugegraph-seatunnel-source/"&gt;SeaTunnel Source export and migration guide&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Version requirement: This guide targets SeaTunnel &lt;a href="https://github.com/apache/seatunnel/tree/3.0.0-release"&gt;3.0+&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; All examples use &lt;code&gt;mappings&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://hugegraph-oink.staged.apache.org/docs/images/seatunnel/seatunnel-vs-loader-en.png"&gt;&lt;img class="td-image" src="https://hugegraph-oink.staged.apache.org/docs/images/seatunnel/seatunnel-vs-loader-en.png" alt="Loader imports data directly with graph mappings; SeaTunnel 3.0+ combines Source, Transform, and Sink, and both support JDBC, Kafka, and graph data" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>